WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.000
Ready? Hello everyone. I am Eva Petrova.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.030
I am marketing manager of Ardes.

3
00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:11.430
I've been with the company for more than 7 years.

4
00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:17.030
This year Ardes celebrates its 30th anniversary.

5
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.350
And our core value is still the same, the customer.

6
00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:25.030
We started with just a handful of people.

7
00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:27.990
Today, we are a team of more than 140.

8
00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:32.710
When someone asked me what holds a business together,

9
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:37.790
the marketer in me answered with the seven P's.

10
00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:42.870
Product, price, place, promotion, people, processes,

11
00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:47.710
and physical evidence. But today, we are here to talk about AI.

12
00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:53.800
For us, responsible AI means using it in a way that is useful and

13
00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:57.640
done right. With a focus on people, processes,

14
00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:00.670
and data. That is how growth lasts.

15
00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:05.350
Today, our focus is on three of them.

16
00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:08.870
People, product, and place.

17
00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:14.280
Data is the foundation of all three, and Kristian will take us deeper

18
00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:18.070
into it. Let me share some practical examples.

19
00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:23.680
People. First, people. Behind every campaign,

20
00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:27.430
there is a designer. And in front of it, a customer.

21
00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:33.560
We value the talent of our designers, so we let AI take care of

22
00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:37.990
adapting each visual to every format we need.

23
00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:41.950
Our people should spend their time on ideas,

24
00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:43.790
not on resizing.

25
00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:47.550
And every idea starts with the customer.

26
00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:51.240
What do they need? And how can we help?

27
00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:57.040
Even when a visual is fully made by AI, there is always a person

28
00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:02.362
behind the concept making sure it's clear and useful.

29
00:02:03.332 --> 00:02:08.292
Because our designs are made by people for

30
00:02:08.292 --> 00:02:11.402
people. Product and data.

31
00:02:11.972 --> 00:02:16.362
Second, let us go back to the seven P's and the product.

32
00:02:17.292 --> 00:02:21.892
Online customers cannot touch the product, so the information has to

33
00:02:21.892 --> 00:02:26.962
do that job. We have more than 30,000 products on our website.

34
00:02:27.612 --> 00:02:32.402
And with AI, we write clear, rich content.

35
00:02:33.092 --> 00:02:36.652
Customers find everything in one place and can choose with

36
00:02:36.652 --> 00:02:42.212
confidence. We took the same idea further with a landing page of

37
00:02:42.212 --> 00:02:48.892
TVs. Its goal is simple, to help people find a TV that truly fits

38
00:02:48.892 --> 00:02:54.452
their needs. AI helped us plan the structure and we created a

39
00:02:54.452 --> 00:02:57.682
prototype that our designers brought to life.

40
00:02:58.452 --> 00:03:00.122
We were not chasing sales.

41
00:03:00.732 --> 00:03:04.772
We wanted every customer to have enough information to make a

42
00:03:04.772 --> 00:03:06.642
choice they would be happy with.

43
00:03:07.692 --> 00:03:12.212
The highlight is an interactive tool that shows how much space each

44
00:03:12.212 --> 00:03:16.882
screen size needs, so you can see which TV fits your living room.

45
00:03:17.612 --> 00:03:22.772
And the most important part of all of this is that it is built on

46
00:03:22.772 --> 00:03:26.842
reliable product data. And people check every result.

47
00:03:27.572 --> 00:03:29.892
AI gives us speed and scale.

48
00:03:29.892 --> 00:03:32.122
Our people make sure it's right.

49
00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:37.252
Processes. Third, from the product to the place.

50
00:03:37.252 --> 00:03:42.012
With AI, we have made order processing faster from the moment you

51
00:03:42.012 --> 00:03:45.482
click buy until your order is on its way.

52
00:03:46.332 --> 00:03:51.402
Customers get their products sooner and we have seen a 20% improvement

53
00:03:52.132 --> 00:03:53.032
in capacity.

54
00:03:53.972 --> 00:03:59.452
Responsibility. And finally, being responsible means being open with

55
00:03:59.452 --> 00:04:05.094
our customers. We follow the EU AI Act and we clearly label every

56
00:04:05.094 --> 00:04:07.044
visual fully made by AI.

57
00:04:07.774 --> 00:04:11.934
People have the right to know what they're looking at, because no

58
00:04:11.934 --> 00:04:14.284
technology works without trust.

59
00:04:14.934 --> 00:04:19.094
So, to sum up, people, processes, and data.

60
00:04:19.094 --> 00:04:22.924
For us, when it comes to AI, these three always go together.

61
00:04:23.774 --> 00:04:28.454
And now, Kristian will take you deeper into the data behind all of this

62
00:04:28.454 --> 00:04:31.934
and show you how it turns into real tech solutions.

63
00:04:31.934 --> 00:04:35.804
Thank you. Thank you, Eva.

64
00:04:36.334 --> 00:04:38.774
Hello, everybody, and we're a bit short on time,

65
00:04:38.774 --> 00:04:42.334
so I will just try to be quick.

66
00:04:42.334 --> 00:04:45.564
I'm Kristian, and I'm Chief AI Officer at Ardes,

67
00:04:46.174 --> 00:04:50.524
and I would like to talk about how I actually entered Ardes,

68
00:04:51.294 --> 00:04:56.534
a company that spent over 30 years bringing new technology to

69
00:04:56.534 --> 00:05:03.134
people, because for us, caring about customers only counts

70
00:05:03.134 --> 00:05:06.884
if the processes and data behind it get the same care.

71
00:05:07.534 --> 00:05:09.724
And we have adopted new technology before.

72
00:05:10.854 --> 00:05:17.014
The internet, online shopping, the cloud, they all helped us move

73
00:05:17.014 --> 00:05:24.294
faster. But AI is the first that could help us more easily read

74
00:05:24.294 --> 00:05:26.924
and understand what we have built over the years.

75
00:05:27.454 --> 00:05:33.334
And this is not a tool that you just simply switch on.

76
00:05:33.334 --> 00:05:37.564
You decide very carefully what it is allowed to touch.

77
00:05:39.814 --> 00:05:43.494
Three things we have learned along our way: about data,

78
00:05:43.494 --> 00:05:49.684
about what we ask AI to do, and about the rules.

79
00:05:50.254 --> 00:05:54.974
First is data. Our base data is not the sales.

80
00:05:54.974 --> 00:05:59.724
It's what we already know as knowledge about the technology.

81
00:06:00.734 --> 00:06:07.135
And these are simple questions: what fits what,

82
00:06:07.135 --> 00:06:12.935
which machine best suits which use case, what is important for a person

83
00:06:12.935 --> 00:06:15.285
to decide on a purchase, and so on.

84
00:06:16.575 --> 00:06:21.815
And we thought that we could make this knowledge more usable,

85
00:06:21.815 --> 00:06:23.685
more accessible for us internally.

86
00:06:24.975 --> 00:06:29.855
And we meant the entire knowledge that we have,

87
00:06:29.855 --> 00:06:32.325
all years of it. So,

88
00:06:36.455 --> 00:06:39.125
What can I say?

89
00:06:41.775 --> 00:06:45.135
All of this knowledge lived in internal documents,

90
00:06:45.135 --> 00:06:48.895
in the reports, and in the heads of people who remember,

91
00:06:48.895 --> 00:06:51.935
unfortunately. And in order to find an answer,

92
00:06:51.935 --> 00:06:53.525
you had to know whom to ask.

93
00:06:54.255 --> 00:07:01.015
And I want to shorten

94
00:07:01.015 --> 00:07:03.765
a little bit. Basically,

95
00:07:04.895 --> 00:07:06.005
to find that answer,

96
00:07:06.975 --> 00:07:10.495
as I told you, you have to know whom to ask,

97
00:07:10.495 --> 00:07:14.125
and no person can read all of that data, but AI can.

98
00:07:14.895 --> 00:07:19.975
And so, for the first time, all of that can be more easily read and

99
00:07:19.975 --> 00:07:22.295
analyzed in one internal system.

100
00:07:22.295 --> 00:07:26.975
Everything that lived in people's heads gets written down first,

101
00:07:26.975 --> 00:07:31.925
that's very important, and all of those years of knowledge became,

102
00:07:32.375 --> 00:07:38.335
rather than an archive, an internal memory that all colleagues can

103
00:07:38.335 --> 00:07:41.695
use. When a colleague learns something,

104
00:07:41.695 --> 00:07:43.245
all colleagues can use it.

105
00:07:44.095 --> 00:07:46.685
And that's where the responsibility starts.

106
00:07:47.495 --> 00:07:54.495
Because we decided on a few things before anything even

107
00:07:54.495 --> 00:07:59.245
went near a model. First, we

108
00:08:01.455 --> 00:08:05.495
let it read only the things that we know about technology,

109
00:08:05.495 --> 00:08:10.417
nothing more. And a dedicated team decides what goes in, because if

110
00:08:10.417 --> 00:08:13.977
we need to be honest, as you probably know, 30 years of experience

111
00:08:13.977 --> 00:08:16.567
also includes 30 years of mistakes.

112
00:08:17.457 --> 00:08:22.657
And the second lesson is that AI goes exactly after the goal you

113
00:08:22.657 --> 00:08:27.007
give it. So, the responsible question is what goal you give it?

114
00:08:27.657 --> 00:08:30.607
And this is what we aim for with the help of AI.

115
00:08:31.097 --> 00:08:34.057
For example, the concept not of a bigger basket,

116
00:08:34.057 --> 00:08:37.777
but the right basket. And sometimes the right basket includes a

117
00:08:37.777 --> 00:08:41.087
cheaper product, but when a colleague knows exactly why,

118
00:08:41.657 --> 00:08:43.327
he can say so with confidence.

119
00:08:45.057 --> 00:08:48.897
Ask AI to help you sell more, and you can see the decisions that

120
00:08:48.897 --> 00:08:51.097
the team starts to push a little bit.

121
00:08:51.097 --> 00:08:57.167
Ask AI to do the right thing, and those decisions start to

122
00:08:58.217 --> 00:09:02.287
matter for the customer in terms of what you stock,

123
00:09:02.817 --> 00:09:04.887
what you advise, and how you fix a problem.

124
00:09:05.457 --> 00:09:08.377
We started with that vision before we built anything,

125
00:09:08.377 --> 00:09:10.007
and the person remains responsible.

126
00:09:12.457 --> 00:09:17.897
Third is the rules. The European AI Act is not an enemy of

127
00:09:17.897 --> 00:09:20.337
a good brand, and for us, a serious one,

128
00:09:20.337 --> 00:09:22.607
it's like a description of it.

129
00:09:23.137 --> 00:09:26.697
And what the law asks here is mostly common sense.

130
00:09:26.697 --> 00:09:29.327
Know what you are using, what tools you are using.

131
00:09:30.337 --> 00:09:36.217
Be honest with people when a machine is involved in

132
00:09:36.217 --> 00:09:39.057
the system, and keep a person always responsible,

133
00:09:39.057 --> 00:09:40.857
not the algorithm behind it.

134
00:09:40.857 --> 00:09:45.297
And help your own team understand the tools that they're already

135
00:09:45.297 --> 00:09:47.487
using before introducing new ones.

136
00:09:47.937 --> 00:09:53.097
And for 30 years we have been selling products that came with rules,

137
00:09:53.097 --> 00:09:55.807
warranty, safety, customer

138
00:09:57.017 --> 00:10:01.567
security about that. And we never thought about this like a

139
00:10:02.097 --> 00:10:05.007
harm to being a good brand.

140
00:10:05.817 --> 00:10:10.378
And for us they're part of the reason why people trust us when they buy

141
00:10:10.378 --> 00:10:14.658
from us. Each one of you is probably hearing the same

142
00:10:14.658 --> 00:10:16.938
questions over and over again these days.

143
00:10:16.938 --> 00:10:18.858
What is AI? How do we use it?

144
00:10:18.858 --> 00:10:21.378
What is AI adoption? How do we measure it?

145
00:10:21.378 --> 00:10:26.418
How do we achieve it? And at Ardes we decided to think very carefully

146
00:10:26.418 --> 00:10:30.648
about that and, honestly, this is my advice to you.

147
00:10:31.058 --> 00:10:33.608
The tools are available to everyone, and

148
00:10:35.098 --> 00:10:38.618
what makes the difference are the three questions that no tool

149
00:10:38.618 --> 00:10:41.928
can answer for you. What your company already knows,

150
00:10:42.418 --> 00:10:47.698
what it is good at, and what you ask AI to help you with,

151
00:10:47.698 --> 00:10:49.648
and who answers for the result?

152
00:10:50.298 --> 00:10:54.808
I believe that in a few years not many people will remember

153
00:10:55.898 --> 00:11:01.938
which company adopted AI first, but for us the customers and

154
00:11:01.938 --> 00:11:05.058
your partners will remember who they still can trust.

155
00:11:05.058 --> 00:11:07.048
Be that company. Thank you.
